--- body ---
## Context
Author decision relayed by the git-erg session (2026-11-09): the harness drives the rollout of
required ID claims (git-erg 0306/0307) to every erg store on padme and doudou. Pin, not release:
every repo takes the binary with sha256
`6a10426263e7571a054557df8965229c92fb87540b07059279f3d20f56c58991` (git-erg rev 2d0dbea,
commit ab519a3; moved by author decision 2026-11-09 from dafb1d48/8d24e74, which forced --no-verify); if git-erg main has moved, stop and ask git-erg. A signed release comes later.
git-erg's dry run on scratch copies: all 25 stores migrate, zero blockers.

## Recipe (one PR per repo, one host, fresh worktree)
1. fetch; skip if origin/main already has `tickets/.claims/`
2. `tickets/erg sync --upstream` (binaries 2c490b7 and later: harness, arena, sen-causal-reading);
   older binaries have no `sync` (it prints help, exits 1): run
   `ERG_UPDATE_URL=https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/git-erg.git tickets/erg update` instead
   (63b5e92: swz, AEDIST, fuzzy-corpus, JETP-observer, chemin-de-voix, climate-finance-het, padme;
   616b023: DOIfetch; 5158508: archiveCIRED; 8331a94: cadens; doudou-only repos: check
   `tickets/erg --help`). 3. check `tickets/erg version` shows the sha256
4. `tickets/erg migrate --claims tickets`; 5. `tickets/erg init` (a locally edited `.ergrc` is kept; one WARN stays)
6. `tickets/erg install --hooks` (rewrites an old managed block, so the commit passes; no --no-verify);
   tracked core.hooksPath: stage the hook change in the PR worktree, review the chaining
7. the repo's own gate; 8. right before merging, merge (or rebase onto) the default branch
   and re-run `tickets/erg migrate --claims tickets`, commit new claims (JETP race: a ticket
   merged meanwhile left main failing check, and the pre-commit block then refused every
   commit); then merge by the repo's process.
After landing: every other clone pulls; per-clone hooks run `tickets/erg install --hooks`.
Branch cut before migration: rebase, `tickets/erg migrate --claims tickets`, commit. Duplicate
number: migrate lists it and writes nothing; renumber one by hand, rerun.
Each repo's migration runs under that repo's own rules (rules/workflow.md, Cross-project work):
its own session, or one launched there; the harness tracks, it does not edit other repos.

